{
  "id": 10,
  "title": "Daily routine",
  "goal": "Describe your daily routine and habits, and say what you and others are doing right now.",
  "intro": "This unit introduces the heart of the Telugu verb. The **non-past** form (*చేస్తాను*, chēstānu) covers both habits ('I do') and the future ('I will do'). The **continuous** form (*చేస్తున్నాను*, chēstunnānu) is for things happening now.\n\nBoth take the same set of **person endings**, which you have already met with ఉండు: -ānu (I), -āvu (you inf.), -āḍu (he), -undi (she/it), -āmu (we), -āru (you pol./they), -āyi (things).",
